{"lines": ["A radio station has buzzed about twenty-five times a minute, day and night, since at least 1982. Nobody will say who runs it.", "Hobbyists call it the Buzzer. Just a flat tone on 4625 kilohertz. Sometimes a man's voice cuts in, reading names and numbers.", "In 2010 it broke. On August twenty-fifth: silence. Then knocks. Shuffling. As if someone stepped into the room.", "Two weeks later, a voice announced a new call sign.", "And that's not the strangest part. At its old tower, a writer found a door ajar, and a black hole where a ladder should be.", "Drop a rock in, and it takes a second to land. Outside, a dog was tied up. Someone feeds it.", "Russia's military has never confirmed it's theirs. So who is in that room, and who is it talking to? Tell me below."], "words": [["A", 0.0, 0.06], ["radio", 0.06, 0.32], ["station", 0.32, 0.72], ["has", 0.72, 1.2], ["buzzed", 1.2, 1.66], ["about", 1.66, 1.78], ["twenty-five", 1.78, 2.22], ["times", 2.22, 2.8], ["a", 2.8, 3.04], ["minute,", 3.04, 3.22], ["day", 3.6, 3.84], ["and", 3.84, 4.12], ["night,", 4.12, 4.36], ["since", 4.78, 4.98], ["at", 4.98, 5.14], ["least", 5.14, 5.24], ["1982.", 5.24, 5.8], ["Nobody", 7.32, 7.7], ["will", 7.7, 8.0], ["say", 8.0, 8.28], ["who", 8.28, 8.56], ["runs", 8.56, 8.82], ["it.", 8.82, 9.1], ["Hobbyists", 9.64, 9.98], ["call", 9.98, 10.32], ["it", 10.32, 10.54], ["the", 10.54, 10.64], ["Buzzer.", 10.64, 11.02], ["Just", 11.58, 11.72], ["a", 11.72, 11.88], ["flat", 11.88, 12.1], ["tone", 12.1, 12.52], ["on", 12.52, 12.9], ["4625", 12.9, 14.3], ["kilohertz.", 14.3, 15.68], ["Sometimes", 16.18, 16.6], ["a", 16.6, 16.92], ["man's", 16.92, 17.38], ["voice", 17.38, 17.66], ["cuts", 17.66, 18.02], ["in,", 18.02, 18.36], ["reading", 18.6, 18.92], ["names", 18.92, 19.36], ["and", 19.36, 19.76], ["numbers.", 19.76, 20.1], ["In", 20.639, 20.72], ["2010", 20.72, 21.16], ["it", 21.16, 21.86], ["broke.", 21.86, 22.12], ["On", 23.0, 23.04], ["August", 23.04, 23.3], ["twenty-fifth:", 23.3, 24.44],